  <img decoding="async" width="768" height="432" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Apple Cofounder Steve Wozniak Says Bitcoin Is a 'Mathematical Miracle'" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-696x385.jpg 696w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-747x420.jpg 747w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-190x107.jpg 190w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-380x214.jpg 380w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz-760x428.jpg 760w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/woz.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>Presenting at the Talent Land Jalisco 2021, Apple cofounder Steve Wozniak called bitcoin an “amazing mathematical miracle.” Wozniak said he’s not a bitcoin investor per se, but “believes in it for the future.”</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Steve Wozniak Is Not Necessarily Invested but Still Believes Bitcoin Is an ‘Amazing Mathematical’ Creation
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">Apple cofounder Steve Wozniak is a fan of bitcoin and he’s mentioned the subject on numerous occasions over the years. Back in August 2018, Wozniak revealed he was participating with a crypto startup and spoke highly about bitcoin. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">“It’s so independent,” Wozniak </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">said</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> at the time. “It’s kind of like the internet when it was brand new… I was amazed at the technology behind it,” Wozniak added. Still months before the internet comparison, Wozniak told an audience at the Nordic Business Forum in Sweden that he wasn’t obsessed with bitcoin either.</span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">“I had bitcoin to experiment with and when it shot up high, I said, ‘I don’t want to become one of those people that watches it, watches it and cares about the number,’” Wozniak said at the time. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Speaking at the Talent Land Jalisco 2021 event this week, Wozniak had a similar outlook and highlighted that he doesn’t invest in bitcoin. The event which was 100% in digital format, saw more than two million attendees dedicated to the development of technology, innovation, and entrepreneurship projects.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Despite not investing in bitcoin, Wozniak said that the leading cryptocurrency was still a very profound invention. Wozniak further stated:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Bitcoin is the most amazing mathematical miracle.
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Wozniak’s Efforce Crypto Coin and His Failed Battle With Google
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">Steve Wozniak also has a cryptocurrency that bears his name called </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">WOZX</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and the crypto asset was developed by the Efforce team and Wozniak. WOZX was developed “as the energy savings token to allow contributors of the Efforce platform to benefit from the energy savings generated by efficiency projects worldwide.” </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    WOZX currently trades for 0.00002146 BTC or roughly $0.719 per unit at the time of writing. The market cap on Friday is hovering above $82 million and has made some gains in recent times. Two-week stats recorded on Friday at 2:00 p.m. (EDT) show WOZX has gained 43.3% in two weeks and 14.0% in a month’s time.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Last year in July, Steve Wozniak and 17 other victims sued Google and its subsidiary Youtube for allowing crypto scams using his name. However, less than 12 months later, Wozniak failed to win the lawsuit against Youtube and its parent, Google LLC.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about Apple cofounder Steve Wozniak saying bitcoin is a mathematical miracle? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below. </strong></em>
  </p>
